Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 02:57:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feature: add InverseGaussian (Wald) distribution

Adds InverseGaussian(mean=1.0, shape=1.0), a direct wrap of
scipy.stats.invgauss, parameterized by the textbook (mean, shape)
convention rather than scipy's own standardized shape parameter (the
translation is mu=mean/shape, scale=shape). Exported from
symbulate/__init__.py; tests added covering mean/variance formulas,
pdf agreement with scipy, the Normal limit as shape grows, error
handling, and plotting.
---
